-- The root (MMS-521): the one place to ask what the law gives. For each pay
-- item it imports every instrument that speaks to it, gathers what each
-- says for a case (its claim, stated in the shared vocabulary), and asks
-- precedence (l4/lib/precedence.l4, encoded once) which one governs and by
-- which rule. The calculator, the contradictions page and any other query
-- ask this module, and an instrument's claim is never the answer by itself.
--
-- Where two or more instruments give different answers for an item and a
-- case, that is a contradiction. The build stays red until the root names
-- its resolution — which instrument governs and by which rule — and the
-- ruling precedence computes agrees with it: `unresolved contradictions`,
-- one list for every item and every number of sources, is asserted empty.
-- The disagreement itself stays asserted as evidence beside it.
--
-- Nothing here is about one item: an item is a `pay item` of the shared
-- vocabulary, and every function takes it. The first item is the 2008
-- supplement (takanon §1.1ג, the agreement of 24.1.2008, owners' circulars
-- תשס"ט/3 and תש"ע/2); its resolutions below are data about it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT precedence
IMPORT `takanon-root`
IMPORT `agreements-root`
IMPORT `circulars-root`

§ `השורש — מקור אחד לשאלה מה הדין נותן`

§§ `המסמכים`

-- The instruments, and what each says, are registered in the collections'
-- roots: l4/lib/takanon-root.l4, l4/lib/agreements-root.l4 and
-- l4/lib/circulars-root.l4. This module asks them, in that order.

§§ `השאלה`

-- Every instrument that speaks to an item, and what it says for a case:
-- the takanon's, the agreements' and the circulars' claims.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A LIST OF `claim`
DECIDE `the claims on` i c IS
    concat (LIST `the takanon's claims on` i c,
                 `the agreements' claims on` i c,
                 `the circulars' claims on` i c)

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling on the item` i c IS
    `the ruling on` (`the claims on` i c) (c's `employer`) (`the date the takanon's provision on it was last amended` i)

@export What a teaching employee is owed for a pay item in a salary month, after precedence between every instrument that speaks to it; nothing where no instrument speaks
GIVEN i IS A `pay item` @desc the pay item asked about
      c IS A `teaching case` @desc the salary month, the employer, the division, the union, and the salary components the item needs
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the answer that governs` i c IS
    CONSIDER `the ruling on the item` i c
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `the answer`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- The items asked about, each checked over the cases below.
`the items` MEANS LIST `the 2008 public-sector supplement`

§§ `מקרים`

-- A case with salary components that make every instrument's arithmetic
-- visible: a combined salary of 10,000 in December 2007 raised by the 4% of
-- January 2008, and תוספת 2001 at 3% of it.
GIVEN `salary month` IS A DATE
      employer IS A `the teacher's employer`
      `post-primary` IS A BOOLEAN
      upper IS A BOOLEAN
      organised IS A BOOLEAN
      `put off` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `teaching case`
DECIDE `a teacher` `salary month` employer `post-primary` upper organised `put off` IS
    `teaching case` WITH
        `the salary month`                IS `salary month`
        `employer`                        IS employer
        `in post-primary education`       IS `post-primary`
        `in the upper division`           IS upper
        `represented by the secondary teachers' organisation` IS organised
        `in a population whose 5% step was put off` IS `put off`
        `combined salary today`           IS 10400
        `supplement 2001 today`           IS 312
        `combined salary in December 2007` IS 10000
        `supplement 2001 in December 2007` IS 300

-- The cases every contradiction is looked for in: the salary months on
-- which some instrument starts or changes, and every combination of the
-- facts the instruments tell teachers apart by.
`the salary months checked` MEANS
    LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2008, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2008, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008,
         DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2009, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2009, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2010,
         DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2011

`the employers checked` MEANS
    LIST `employed by the State`, `employed by a local authority`, `employed by another owning body`

-- For a month and an employer, every combination of the facts the
-- instruments ask about: outside post-primary education the division and
-- the organisation do not arise.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, e IS A `the teacher's employer`
GIVETH A LIST OF `teaching case`
DECIDE `the cases for` d e IS
    LIST `a teacher` d e FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE,
         `a teacher` d e FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE,
         `a teacher` d e TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE,
         `a teacher` d e TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE,
         `a teacher` d e TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE,
         `a teacher` d e TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE,
         `a teacher` d e TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE,
         `a teacher` d e TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE,
         `a teacher` d e TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE,
         `a teacher` d e TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `teaching case`
DECIDE `the cases in` d IS
    concat (map (GIVEN e YIELD `the cases for` d e) `the employers checked`)

`the cases checked` MEANS
    concat (map `the cases in` `the salary months checked`)

§§ `סתירות`

@desc A contradiction: for an item and a case, the instruments that speak give two or more answers.
DECLARE `contradiction` HAS
    `item`     IS A `pay item`
    `sources`  IS A LIST OF STRING @desc the modules of every instrument that speaks, in the root's order
    `answers`  IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc each answer given, once
    `the ruling` IS A `ruling`

@desc How the root settles a contradiction: which instrument governs and by which rule.
DECLARE `resolution` HAS
    `item`           IS A `pay item`
    `sources`        IS A LIST OF STRING
    `governed by`    IS A STRING @desc the module of the instrument that governs
    `by the rule`    IS A STRING

GIVEN item IS A `pay item`
      claims IS A LIST OF `claim`
      r IS A MAYBE `ruling`
GIVETH A LIST OF `contradiction`
DECIDE `the contradiction in` item claims r IS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST governing THEN
        IF count (nub (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `answer`) claims)) AT LEAST 2
        THEN LIST (`contradiction` WITH
                      `item`    IS item
                      `sources` IS map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `by`'s `module`) claims
                      `answers` IS nub (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `answer`) claims)
                      `the ruling` IS governing)
        ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A LIST OF `contradiction`
DECIDE `the contradictions on` i c IS
    `the contradiction in` i (`the claims on` i c) (`the ruling on the item` i c)

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`
GIVETH A LIST OF `contradiction`
DECIDE `the contradictions on the item` i IS
    concat (map (GIVEN c YIELD `the contradictions on` i c) `the cases checked`)

`the contradictions` MEANS
    concat (map `the contradictions on the item` `the items`)

-- The resolutions: one for each set of instruments that disagree and the
-- instrument precedence makes govern them. Each names the rule; the gate
-- below holds precedence to it.
GIVEN item IS A `pay item`
      sources IS A LIST OF STRING
      `governed by` IS A STRING
      rule IS A STRING
GIVETH A `resolution`
DECIDE `resolved` item sources `governed by` rule IS
    `resolution` WITH `item` IS item, `sources` IS sources, `governed by` IS `governed by`, `by the rule` IS rule

GIVEN instruments IS A LIST OF `instrument`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `the modules of` instruments IS
    map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `module`) instruments

`the resolutions` MEANS
    LIST `the takanon against the agreement`,
         `the takanon against circular תשס"ט/3`,
         `the takanon, the agreement and circular תשס"ט/3`,
         `the takanon against both circulars`,
         `all four on the 2008 supplement`

-- A state (or local-authority) post-primary teacher of the organisation:
-- the takanon's 5% of today's combined salary from 1.1.2010, against the
-- agreement's 5% of the December 2007 values from the salary of December
-- 2009. The takanon's introduction makes a collective agreement prevail
-- over it (the card takanon-2008).
`the takanon against the agreement` MEANS
    `resolved` `the 2008 public-sector supplement`
        (`the modules of` (LIST `the takanon §1.1`, `the agreement of 24.1.2008`))
        (`the agreement of 24.1.2008`'s `module`)
        `the takanon's introduction: an agreement prevails`

-- An owner's teacher whom the agreement does not cover (not of the
-- organisation, or employed by an owner that is not a local authority):
-- the takanon against תשס"ט/3's 2.88% of today's values. The circular
-- (14.12.2008) is not more recent than §1.1 as updated on 2.2.2010, so by
-- the takanon's own introduction it does not prevail, and nothing else that
-- prevails over the takanon speaks.
`the takanon against circular תשס"ט/3` MEANS
    `resolved` `the 2008 public-sector supplement`
        (`the modules of` (LIST `the takanon §1.1`, `circular תשס"ט/3`))
        (`the takanon §1.1`'s `module`)
        `the takanon's introduction: nothing that prevails over it speaks`

-- A local authority's post-primary teacher of the organisation, outside
-- the upper division (or in it before December 2009): the agreement puts
-- the takanon out; תשס"ט/3's 2.88% of today's values is below the
-- agreement's 3% of December 2007's, and a circular does not out-rank the
-- agreement it carries out (the finding F-2008-09_tashsat_03-a).
`the takanon, the agreement and circular תשס"ט/3` MEANS
    `resolved` `the 2008 public-sector supplement`
        (`the modules of` (LIST `the takanon §1.1`, `the agreement of 24.1.2008`, `circular תשס"ט/3`))
        (`the agreement of 24.1.2008`'s `module`)
        `a circular never out-ranks the agreement`

-- An owner's upper-division teacher the agreement does not cover, from
-- December 2009: neither circular is more recent than §1.1 as updated on
-- 2.2.2010, so the takanon stands over both.
`the takanon against both circulars` MEANS
    `resolved` `the 2008 public-sector supplement`
        (`the modules of` (LIST `the takanon §1.1`, `circular תשס"ט/3`, `circular תש"ע/2`))
        (`the takanon §1.1`'s `module`)
        `the takanon's introduction: nothing that prevails over it speaks`

-- A local authority's upper-division teacher of the organisation, from
-- December 2009: all four speak (the card supplement-2008). The agreement
-- puts the takanon out; of the circulars the later, תש"ע/2, replaces
-- תשס"ט/3; its printed 4.81% of today's values is above the agreement's 5%
-- of December 2007's, approved by the Treasury so §29 leaves it, and §22
-- lets a term in the employee's favour stand.
`all four on the 2008 supplement` MEANS
    `resolved` `the 2008 public-sector supplement`
        (`the modules of` (LIST `the takanon §1.1`, `the agreement of 24.1.2008`, `circular תשס"ט/3`, `circular תש"ע/2`))
        (`circular תש"ע/2`'s `module`)
        `§22: a term in the employee's favour stands`

GIVEN x IS A `contradiction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is resolved` x IF
    any (GIVEN r YIELD `settles` r x) `the resolutions`

GIVEN x IS A `contradiction`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the contradiction's name` x IS
    CONCAT `the name of the item` (x's `item`), ": ", `the sources joined` (x's `sources`), " — ", x's `the ruling`'s `governed by`'s `module`, " ", x's `the ruling`'s `by the rule`

GIVEN names IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the sources joined` names IS
    foldr (GIVEN n, acc YIELD IF acc EQUALS "" THEN n ELSE CONCAT n, ", ", acc) "" names

`unresolved contradictions` MEANS
    nub (map `the contradiction's name` (filter (GIVEN x YIELD NOT `is resolved` x) `the contradictions`))

#EVAL `unresolved contradictions`
#ASSERT null `unresolved contradictions`

§§ `הדוח`

-- What the site's page of this module shows (tools/roots.py): each
-- resolution, the instruments it settles by their names, which governs, by
-- which rule, and in how many of the cases checked.
`the instruments` MEANS
    concat (LIST `the takanon's instruments`, `the agreements' instruments`, `the circulars' instruments`)

GIVEN m IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the title of` m IS
    foldr (GIVEN i, acc YIELD IF i's `module` EQUALS m THEN i's `title` ELSE acc) m `the instruments`

GIVEN r IS A `resolution`, x IS A `contradiction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `settles` r x IF
        r's `item` EQUALS x's `item`
    AND r's `sources` EQUALS x's `sources`
    AND r's `governed by` EQUALS x's `the ruling`'s `governed by`'s `module`
    AND r's `by the rule` EQUALS x's `the ruling`'s `by the rule`

GIVEN r IS A `resolution`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the report line of` r IS
    CONCAT `the name of the item` (r's `item`), " | ",
           `the titles joined` (map `the title of` (r's `sources`)), " | ",
           `the title of` (r's `governed by`), " | ",
           r's `by the rule`, " | ",
           TOSTRING (count (filter (GIVEN x YIELD `settles` r x) `the contradictions`))

GIVEN titles IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the titles joined` titles IS
    foldr (GIVEN n, acc YIELD IF acc EQUALS "" THEN n ELSE CONCAT n, " · ", acc) "" titles

`the resolutions report` MEANS
    map `the report line of` `the resolutions`

#EVAL `the resolutions report`
#EVAL count `the cases checked`

§§ `ראיות`

-- The disagreements themselves, asserted as evidence: each holds while the
-- instruments disagree and goes red if one of them is ever brought into
-- line, so the resolution above is looked at again.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the answers on` i c IS
    map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `answer`) (`the claims on` i c)

#ASSERT ((`the answers on` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` (`a teacher` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2010) `employed by a local authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
    EQUALS LIST 520, 515, 308.5056, 515.2472)
#ASSERT ((`the answer that governs` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` (`a teacher` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2010) `employed by a local authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
    EQUALS JUST 515.2472)
#ASSERT ((`the answers on` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` (`a teacher` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2010) `employed by the State` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
    EQUALS LIST 520, 515)
#ASSERT ((`the answer that governs` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` (`a teacher` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2010) `employed by the State` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
    EQUALS JUST 515)
#ASSERT ((`the answers on` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` (`a teacher` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008) `employed by a local authority` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
    EQUALS LIST 156, 309, 308.5056)
#ASSERT ((`the answer that governs` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` (`a teacher` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008) `employed by a local authority` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
    EQUALS JUST 309)
#ASSERT ((`the answers on` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` (`a teacher` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2010) `employed by another owning body` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
    EQUALS LIST 520, 308.5056, 515.2472)
#ASSERT ((`the answer that governs` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` (`a teacher` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2010) `employed by another owning body` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
    EQUALS JUST 520)
-- Where one instrument speaks there is nothing to resolve: a state
-- primary teacher has only the takanon.
#ASSERT ((`the answers on` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` (`a teacher` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2010) `employed by the State` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
    EQUALS LIST 520)
